{"name":"Plum Cake","hex":"#d1bfdc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"plum cake","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of plumcake."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plum_cake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Plum cake","blocks":[{"text":"Plum cake refers to a wide range of cakes usually made with dried fruits such as currants, raisins, sultanas, or prunes, and also sometimes with fresh fruits. There is a wide range of popular plum cakes and puddings. Since the meaning of the word \"plum\" has changed over time, many items referred to as plum cakes and popular in England since at least the eighteenth century have now become known as fruitcake. The English variety of plum cake also exists on the European mainland, but may vary in ingredients and consistency. British colonists and missionaries brought the dried fruit variety of cake with them, for example, in British India where it was served around the time of the Christmas holiday season. In America's Thirteen Colonies, where it became associated with elections, one version came to be called election cake."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Plum_cake_08_ies.jpg/330px-Plum_cake_08_ies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plum_cake","wikidata":"Q3906768"},{"title":"Plum","blocks":[{"text":"A plum is a fruit of some species in Prunus subg. Prunus. Dried plums are usually called prunes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Plums_African_Rose_-_whole%2C_halved_and_slice.jpg/330px-Plums_African_Rose_-_whole%2C_halved_and_slice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plum","wikidata":"Q12372598"},{"title":"Cake","blocks":[{"text":"Cake is a baker's confectionery made by combining flour with a liquid, a fat or both, and usually with a leavening agent. Cakes are usually baked, but can be griddled. In their oldest forms, cakes were modifications of bread, but cakes now cover a wide range of preparations that can be simple or elaborate and which share features with other desserts such as pastries, meringues, custards, and pies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Pound_layer_cake.jpg/330px-Pound_layer_cake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cake","wikidata":"Q13276"},{"title":"Plum (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Plum is a purple color with a brownish-gray tinge, like that shown on the right, or a reddish purple, which is a close representation of the average color of the plum fruit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Plum_on_tree02.jpg/330px-Plum_on_tree02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plum_(color)","wikidata":"Q3108722"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Baskidische_Pflaumenkuchen..JPG/500px-Baskidische_Pflaumenkuchen..JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Baskidische_Pflaumenkuchen..JPG/1280px-Baskidische_Pflaumenkuchen..JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Baskidische_Pflaumenkuchen..JPG/500px-Baskidische_Pflaumenkuchen..JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Slices of plum cake with a plum filling","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABaskidische_Pflaumenkuchen..JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/World%27s_Best_Fruitcake_Katya_Creates_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg/500px-World%27s_Best_Fruitcake_Katya_Creates_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&ut